## Getting started

```bash
cp .env.example .env
go mod tidy
{{- if .UseDocker}}
docker compose up -d      # starts {{.Database}}{{if .UseRedis}} + redis{{end}}
{{- end}}
go run ./cmd/server
```

Health check: `GET /healthz`

{{- if .UseAuth}}

## Auth

{{if eq .AuthType "jwt"}}
JWT auth lives in `internal/auth`. Claims are built around an extensible
`Claims` struct — add whatever custom fields (scopes, tenant id, roles...)
you need in `internal/auth/claims.go` without touching the issuing/parsing
logic.

Routes: `POST /auth/register`, `POST /auth/login`, `POST /auth/refresh`.
Protect a route with the `auth.RequireAuth` middleware and read the claims
back out with `auth.ClaimsFromContext(ctx)`.
{{else}}
Session auth lives in `internal/auth`. Session data is a `map[string]any`
under the hood (`internal/auth/session.go`) so you can stash arbitrary
extra fields (roles, tenant id, whatever) with `sess.Set("key", value)`
and read them back with `sess.Get("key")`.

Routes: `POST /auth/register`, `POST /auth/login`, `POST /auth/logout`.
Protect a route with the `auth.RequireAuth` middleware.
{{end}}
{{- if .UseOAuth}}
OAuth ({{range $i, $p := .OAuthProviders}}{{if $i}}, {{end}}{{$p}}{{end}}) is wired through
[markbates/goth](https://github.com/markbates/goth). Fill in the
`*_CLIENT_ID` / `*_CLIENT_SECRET` env vars, then hit
`GET /auth/{provider}` to kick off a flow and
`GET /auth/{provider}/callback` to complete it — on success it issues the
same {{.AuthType}} the rest of the app uses.
{{- end}}
{{- end}}

